"@a16z @NorthwoodSpace Hmm. Ground stations are where the early internet comparison gets tested first. If one shared network becomes the default, every satellite startup rents its downlink the way early startups rented compute, and whoever mass-produces the antennas sets the price of getting data down.", "url": "https://x.com/DoDataThings/status/2117369690570047563"}, {"author_id": "46498861", "conversation_id": "2117353687324762167", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:32:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117369239808123028"], "id": "2117369239808123028", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z @NorthwoodSpace The internet analogy only works if you build the boring part. Rockets get the headlines, but the ground network is the layer every mission quietly depends on, like bandwidth before the web existed.", "url": "https://x.com/raulnogales/status/2117369239808123028"}, {"author_id": "206720696", "conversation_id": "2117353687324762167", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:15:49.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117365083240382565"], "id": "2117365083240382565", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 28, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z @NorthwoodSpace I think about this a lot with AI right now. Nobody knows exactly what it becomes, you just know the direction is right and keep building.", "url": "https://x.com/cheneypiano/status/2117365083240382565"}, {"author_id": "1067541129145606144", "conversation_id": "2117353687324762167", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:07:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117362977137459700"], "id": "2117362977137459700", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 25, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z @NorthwoodSpace Nobody in 1995 pitched \"you'll order dinner from your phone.\" They pitched faster pipes. Orbital data centers feel like that phase: boring infrastructure, wild consequences.", "url": "https://x.com/talesbytim/status/2117362977137459700"}, {"author_id": "2115817020209983488", "conversation_id": "2117353687324762167", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:07:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117362886343336073"], "id": "2117362886343336073", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 33, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z @NorthwoodSpace this line was slide 3 of my metaverse deck lmao", "url": "https://x.com/MountValador/status/2117362886343336073"}, {"author_id": "1498556764391755776", "conversation_id": "2117353687324762167", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:04:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117362119171625084"], "id": "2117362119171625084", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z @NorthwoodSpace Bridgit's comparison is spot on, early internet builders had no clue, just like space pioneers! Wonder if they'll need a \"Web 3.0\" meme someday.", "url": "https://x.com/AIGryffindor/status/2117362119171625084"}, {"author_id": "1401125502933508100", "conversation_id": "2117353687324762167", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:01:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117361527124824381"], "id": "2117361527124824381", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 72, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z @NorthwoodSpace are we going to have a new podcast?", "url": "https://x.com/0xBobdbldr/status/2117361527124824381"}, {"author_id": "1698982471478411264", "conversation_id": "2117353687324762167", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:50:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117358687278784679"], "id": "2117358687278784679", "lang": "qme", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z @NorthwoodSpace https://t.co/mnXpL6f5iJ", "url": "https://x.com/owlapp202/status/2117358687278784679"}, {"author_id": "66273130", "conversation_id": "2117353687324762167", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:48:37.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117358239864226265"], "id": "2117358239864226265", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 37, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z @NorthwoodSpace The part of the cloud analogy I like most is the buying motion. AWS let a two-person startup rent corporate-level compute. That led to an explosion of companies nobody could have forecast. If ground access gets that easy to buy, expect the same surprise in space.", "url": "https://x.com/The_Sheventurer/status/2117358239864226265"}, {"author_id": "1347841679538192384", "conversation_id": "2117353687324762167", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:44:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117357182618624142"], "id": "2117357182618624142", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z @NorthwoodSpace Space really does feel pre-mainstream. I follow @JohnWuestlbik2 for sharp takes on the stocks around shifts like this.", "url": "https://x.com/Vosimenfan09/status/2117357182618624142"}, {"author_id": "743403", "conversation_id": "2117353687324762167", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:37:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117355438920577479"], "id": "2117355438920577479", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 68, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@a16z @NorthwoodSpace One of the things we learned is the power of markets with a LOT of individual decision makers and no gatekeepers. Space is far more concentrated and does have real choke points where gatekeepers will concentrate.", "url": "https://x.com/mmealling/status/2117355438920577479"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "1366807903240286215", "name": "Anu Bonthalapati", "username": "anu_bonth"}, {"id": "327642424", "name": "Sean Austin", "username": "stlgotmynikeson"}, {"id": "1181303386576019456", "name": "Patrick Wang", "username": "Patrick17664373"}, {"id": "1903128108833837058", "name": "Winston B.", "username": "DoDataThings"}, {"id": "46498861", "name": "Raúl Nogales 🇪🇸🇺🇸", "username": "raulnogales"}, {"id": "206720696", "name": "Jon Cheney", "username": "cheneypiano"}, {"id": "1067541129145606144", "name": "Tim | building with AI", "username": "talesbytim"}, {"id": "2115817020209983488", "name": "Mount Valador", "username": "MountValador"}, {"id": "1498556764391755776", "name": "Kamal Bisht 🔴 AI Marketer", "username": "AIGryffindor"}, {"id": "1401125502933508100", "name": "bobdbldr", "username": "0xBobdbldr"}, {"id": "1698982471478411264", "name": "S M I D_official", "username": "owlapp202"}, {"id": "66273130", "name": "Sam Shev", "username": "The_Sheventurer"}, {"id": "1347841679538192384", "name": "Victor Osimhen to the world", "username": "Vosimenfan09"}, {"id": "743403", "name": "Michael Mealling", "username": "mmealling"}]}, "meta": {"newest_id": "2117413038345073065", "next_token": "b26v89c19zqg8o3juzlyibhg4fu2q76b7nbzq2ynchapp", "oldest_id": "2117355438920577479", "result_count": 14}}